"""
takeda_template_fruzaqla.py — FRUZAQLA brand template (self-contained) + chrome.

Part of the SPLIT build: each brand template lives in its OWN file so a project
loads only the brand(s) it needs. Payloads are gzip-compressed base64, decoded on
import. Importing this module registers FRUZAQLA into the shared registry that
takeda.py reads; then Deck(brand="FRUZAQLA") and apply_fruzaqla_chrome() work.

Provenance (updated — harvested from the FRUZAQLA reference deck
"2025_02_19_-_Fruzaqla_Marketing_Mix_Results_v1_0.pptx"):
  * THEME: the reference deck's real "Custom 75" colour scheme is now baked into
    every theme part of the embedded template, so schemeClr references resolve to
    the genuine FRUZAQLA palette:
        accent1 = 81C44D  lime green      accent4 = 9A4398  purple
        accent2 = 01AFD7  cyan            accent5 = 5B9BD5  blue
        accent3 = 074F71  dark teal       accent6 = 70AD47  green
        dk2 = 44546A   lt2 = E7E6E6   (native font: Arial; deck standardises to Aptos)
    NOTE: this REPLACES the earlier invented purple-centric remap
    (9A4398/743272/074F71/BEB7D7/EDD7ED/A3A1A8). The purple is accent4 here, not
    accent1 — the reference deck leads with lime-green/cyan/teal and uses purple as
    a strong secondary (numbered markers, category fills).
  * CHROME — both assets are now the REAL ones from the reference deck:
        FRUQ_BANNER  = the content-slide chrome cropped from the reference deck's
                       content background (image7): a full-width TOP BAND (~1.57" tall)
                       carrying the navy->purple gradient that sweeps into a purple
                       TOP-RIGHT corner wave, with a thin white curved rule below it.
                       Placed at the top and SENT BEHIND content; the body below stays
                       white (matching the reference, whose background is white below
                       the band). Cropped to a band (not full-slide) so the Mode B
                       fidelity audit does not mistake it for a flattened source raster.
        FRUQ_LOGO    = the official "Fruzaqla (fruquintinib) capsules" lockup
                       (image2): multicolour ring + navy wordmark + purple subtitle.
                       Bottom-right, whitespace-contingent. (Previously not shipped —
                       it is now included, so apply_fruzaqla_chrome can place it.)
  * CANVAS: the underlying master/layout geometry remains the shared Takeda 2026
    corporate canvas (40 layouts). The full reference template (4 masters, ~72
    layouts, incl. Japanese-localised) plus its section-divider photography is ~8.4 MB
    of media and exceeds the split-module size budget (~0.9-1.6 MB/brand), so brand
    identity is carried by the real theme + real chrome rather than by embedding the
    whole reference deck. Regenerate with the full deck only if a size increase is
    acceptable.

Reference brand facts (title colour, tables, chart order) live in SKILL.md.

API (identical to the other template modules):
  template_path("FRUZAQLA") -> path to decoded .pptx (gunzipped to /tmp on first call)
  chrome_path("FRUQ_BANNER"|"FRUQ_LOGO") -> path to decoded chrome image
  CHROME_GEOMETRY -> placement geometry, merged into the shared registry on import
"""
